      "confidence": 0.98
    },
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["NAVC2"],
      "pins": ["NAVC2.18", "NAVC2.63", "NAVC2.12", "NAVC2.13"],
      "nets": [
        "Net-(NAVC2-VSS-Pad18)",
        "unconnected-(NAVC2-VSSA-Pad12)",
        "VDDA_NAVC"
      ],
      "observed": "NAVC2 VSS pins 18 and 63 are connected only to each other, not to GND. NAVC2 VSSA pin 12 is unconnected, and VDDA pin 13 is connected only to VDDA_NAVC with a capacitor and no supply connection.",
      "expected": "MCU VSS and VSSA pins must be tied to GND, and VDDA must be connected to the 3.3 V supply with proper decoupling.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"144\") (name \"Net-(NAVC2-VSS-Pad18)\") (class \"Default\") (node (ref \"NAVC2\") (pin \"18\") (pinfunction \"VSS\") (pintype \"power_in\")) (node (ref \"NAVC2\") (pin \"63\") (pinfunction \"VSS\") (pintype \"passive\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"163\") (name \"VDDA_NAVC\") (class \"Default\") (node (ref \"C44\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"NAVC2\") (pin \"13\") (pinfunction \"VDDA\") (pintype \"power_in\")))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The navigation MCU has floating ground and analog supply, preventing normal operation and potentially causing undefined sensor-interface behavior.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["FCC2", "UART3_FCC2", "C92"],
      "pins": [
        "FCC2.48",
        "FCC2.73",
        "UART3_FCC2.3",
        "UART3_FCC2.4",
        "C92.1"
      ],
      "nets": [
        "NET0047",
        "NET0174",
        "unconnected-(C92-Pad1)"
      ],
      "observed": "FCC2 VCAP pins 48 and 73 are connected to UART3_FCC2 connector pins 3 and 4. The 2.2 uF capacitor C92, which would normally decouple a VCAP pin, has its non-ground side left unconnected.",
      "expected": "STM32H7 VCAP pins require low-ESR decoupling capacitors to GND and should not be connected to an external UART connector. UART connector pins should connect to MCU UART GPIOs.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"36\") (name \"NET0047\") (class \"Default\") (node (ref \"FCC2\") (pin \"48\") (pinfunction \"VCAP\") (pintype \"power_out\")) (node (ref \"UART3_FCC2\") (pin \"3\") (pinfunction \"Pin_3\") (pintype \"passive\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"168\") (name \"unconnected-(C92-Pad1)\") (class \"Default\") (node (ref \"C92\") (pin \"1\") (pintype \"passive\")))"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The MCU internal regulator loses its required VCAP decoupling and the UART3 port is miswired, likely causing instability or damage and making that UART unusable.",
      "confidence": 0.9
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The netlist contains major power and connectivity anomalies: the MCU VDD/VSS/VCAP connections are not made as specified, leaving the flight and navigation processors unpowered or improperly decoupled."
}

